Major architectural divergence
------------------------------

The maintained system no longer follows the historical upstream architecture as a synchronization
target. Major project-owned divergence includes:

- Windows-only production support with semantic Photoshop execution routed through the UXP companion;
- an embedded durable Photoshop Guard in the same MCP server process, with required-mode mutation
  control and evidence-bound recovery instead of an external controller/daemon route;
- retirement of ExtendScript/COM/VBS production fallbacks and fail-closed UXP routing for maintained
  semantic mutations;
- a project-owned digital-painting control layer, visual review pipeline, method/stage policy,
  document pinning and source/product identity verification gates.

